lled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production, in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator partial failure, leaving the service mixed (us-east v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west v2.3.1). A retry completed the rollout. Post-rollback status: all regions on v2.3.0, healthy, error rate 0.002. v2.3.1 remains unhealthy and should not be redeployed until fixed. The orchestrator partial failure should be investigated."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out, so I'll check whether it was created before retrying, to avoid a duplicate page.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01BCwLCgDn7jh2TF127A7TVC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it is healthy again (error rate 0.002, down from 0.18). SEV2 incident INC-0001 is open and describes what was done.\n\n- **Rollback target:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 was unhealthy, and v2.3.1-rc was only in staging. Because v2.3.0 was previously healthy in production, no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the service mixed (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). I retried the same rollback once, and it completed across all regions.\n- **Incident:** The first attempt to create the incident timed out. I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so I did not open a duplicate.\n\nFollow-up:\n- The orchestrator partial failure should be investigated, since it could recur on the next rollback.\n- v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until the health check failure is fixed.", "type": "text"}]}]}